Z||000000||wkayl||07-25-2000||10:38 PM||||I talked my wife (of 24 years) to go with me to take the sunroof off an 85GT.  She was not impressed with the "quality" time we spent there.  I think I made a big mistake.  Those 2 hrs are going to cost me many, many hours of shopping.  I don't think it's fair.  When I go to the parts store or Wal-Mart or the grogery store, I know what I want and it only takes me 15 min to get what I want.  She stops and looks at every "pretty" thing that catches her eye.  She can spend 2 hrs just looking at shoes and still not buy any.  She did get some good video of me taking out the top.  I don't think I will take any video of her picking out pillow cases though.  So, as they say, be careful what you wish for, you may get it. ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Monkeyman||07-25-2000||10:47 PM||||Christmas shopping:  Me--In the door to the car-----45 min. (tops).<BR>Her--3 months.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||07-26-2000||08:14 AM||||wkyal,<P>I'm with you, bud! It was 22 years last February. I couldn't drag my wife into a junk yard. She will barely come into my work area in the garage. Heck, she'll bring me out a cup of coffee and set it on the first level surface she can find and then high-tail it out of there.<P><BR>She is a peach though and I wouldn't trade her for anything. She lets me play with my toys about as much as I can stand and, occationally, slips me a few $$$ if I get into a pinch.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> She will ride in the Fiero... if I can find a sitter for the kids.<P>Gotta love that,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||12
Z||000003||1FST2M6||07-26-2000||08:29 AM||||Hope my girlfriend doesn't change... My new GT got here on monday.. and lastnight her and i were taking it all apart to paint it. BlackGT came over, laughin cause she was dirtier than i.  LOVE my girlfriend of over 2 years... helps me change the Clutch/tranny 5 times in my SE. and never ONCE complained...  Todd... you reading this! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||b lo 0||07-26-2000||09:33 AM||||My girlfriend of a year and I have an unwritten understanding.  She plays league softball, and I try to make it to most of her games and practices.  In return, she comes a whole lotta places with me.  In fact, about a month ago, she went with me to the Night of Fire drag races in Commerce and <B>enjoyed herself</B>.  How cool is that?  She is actually supporting my obsession with cars, and shares it to some extent.  She also happens to be beautiful, sexy, and she has a great personality.  Could I get any luckier?  And no, before you ask, you <I>cannot</I> have her!  She's mine!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">  <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Taijiguy||07-26-2000||11:12 AM||||Once upon a time I had a really cool girlfriend who loved to work on cars as much as me. She'd bring her pretty little self out and climb under the thing practically before I could get jack stands under it. Too bad she was such a froot-loop in so many OTHER ways!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>My current girlfriend is WAAAAAAY to prissy to ever work on a car. She doesn't even want to wash her own car......leaves that to me. Fortunately, she makes up for it by being a few other things:<P>A licensed massage therapist<BR>A professional gourmet cook<BR>A regular subscriber to the Victoria's Secret catalogue (and leaaves it for me to look through)<BR>Very easy on the eyes<P>I guesss it's a good trade-off, but sometimes I wonder......   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>-Taiji||||reg||1
